\begin{document}
\maketitle

\begin{abstract}
We measure the thermal efficiency of a rooftop flat-plate solar water
heater across six days of mixed cloud cover.
Efficiency ranges from about one third on the cloudiest day to well
over half on the clearest, with wind the strongest predictor of loss.
\end{abstract}

\section*{Acknowledgements}
\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Acknowledgements}
Thanks to the building custodians for roof access, and to our teaching
assistant for calibrating the pyranometer before the first clear day.

